---
import Layout from "@/layouts/main.astro"

const GEAR = [
  { label: "MACHINE", name: "Sage Barista Express", image: "/coffee/machine.png", colClass: "col-span-6 lg:row-span-6 lg:col-span-6 sm:row-span-2 sm:col-span-2", imgClass: "w-[120%] -bottom-80 -left-40 group-hover:-translate-y-4", headingClass: "text-8xl md:text-8xl", labelSize: "sm" },
  { label: "GRINDER", name: "Fellow Ode", image: "/coffee/grinder.png", colClass: "col-span-3 sm:row-span-1 sm:col-span-1 lg:row-span-3 lg:col-end-10 lg:col-start-7", imgClass: "h-[120%] w-[120%] -bottom-12 -right-24 group-hover:-translate-x-4", headingClass: "text-3xl md:text-5xl", labelSize: "sm" },
  { label: "KETTLE", name: "Fellow Stagg", image: "/coffee/kettle.png", colClass: "col-span-3 lg:row-start-4 sm:row-span-1 sm:col-span-1 lg:row-end-7 lg:col-end-10 lg:col-start-7", imgClass: "w-[137.5%] -right-12 -bottom-16 group-hover:-translate-y-4", headingClass: "text-3xl md:text-5xl", labelSize: "sm" },
  { label: "BREWER", name: "Hario v60", image: "/coffee/v60.webp", colClass: "col-span-2 lg:row-span-2 lg:col-span-2 lg:col-start-10 sm:row-span-1 sm:col-span-1", imgClass: "w-[90%] -right-4 -bottom-9 group-hover:rotate-[10deg] group-hover:-translate-y-2 group-hover:-translate-x-6", headingClass: "", labelSize: "xs" },
  { label: "BREWER", name: "Aeropress", image: "/coffee/aeropress.png", colClass: "col-span-2 lg:row-span-2 lg:col-span-2 lg:col-start-10 sm:row-span-1 sm:col-span-1", imgClass: "w-full rotate-[30deg] -right-8 -bottom-6 group-hover:rotate-[15deg] group-hover:translate-y-2", headingClass: "", labelSize: "xs" },
  { label: "SCALE", name: "Rhino Dosing Scale", image: "/coffee/scale.png", colClass: "col-span-2 lg:row-span-2 lg:col-span-2 lg:col-start-10 sm:row-span-1 sm:col-span-1", imgClass: "w-[120%] -right-12 -bottom-16 scale-x-[-1] group-hover:translate-y-2", headingClass: "", labelSize: "xs" },
]

const PLACES = [
  { name: "Giraffe", country: "Rotterdam, NL", image: "/coffee/places/giraffe.jpeg", score: 4.5 },
  { name: "Qima Café", country: "London, UK", image: "/coffee/places/qima.webp", score: 4.8 },
  { name: "The Coffee Bár", country: "Budapest, HU", image: "/coffee/places/tcb.webp", score: 4.2 },
]
---

<Layout title="Ayoub's Coffee life">
  <header class="container max-w-2xl px-6 pt-32 pb-8 mx-auto mb-24">
    <h1 class="mb-4 text-4xl font-bold leading-snug md:text-5xl md:leading-snug">
      My coffee corner
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm md:text-base md:leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
      Welcome to my little coffee space. Here I plan to share several aspects of my
      coffee discovery journey, from gear and bean reviews to personal thoughts about
      the dive into this beautiful, tasty and crazy rabbit hole. Enjoy your stay,
      possibly while sipping a nice warm cup of java.
    </p>
  </header>

  <!-- BEANS -->
  <section class="overflow-hidden mb-32">
    <header class="container max-w-2xl px-6 mx-auto mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-3xl">
        My Beans
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm md:text-base md:leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Every amazing cup of coffee starts from incredible beans. One aspect I'm loving
        about getting more involved in my coffee consumption is discovering the stories
        behind these wonderful beans. Be it the different preparation techniques, the
        cultural implications of the country they are produced in, the biodiversity
        that's found within this plant's genus and the stories of the people behind them.
      </p>
      <hr class="my-6 border-border" />
      <p class="text-sm md:text-base md:leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Experimenting with different producers and roasters has become a treat I indulge
        in a lot and these are some of the experiences I've had as of lately and some
        of those that I've fell in love in the past months.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="container max-w-2xl px-6 mx-auto">
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground italic">Beans data will be connected soon.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- GEAR -->
  <section class="mb-32">
    <header class="container max-w-2xl px-6 mx-auto mb-8">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-3xl">
        My coffee gear
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm md:text-base md:leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        One incredibly fun (or terrible, depending on the perspective) aspect of getting
        into home brewing is getting to know all of the various tools that are used in
        the space to get ever so closer to brewing some incredible coffee drinks. These
        are the ones I'm currently using in my home barista setup.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="container grid max-w-5xl grid-cols-6 gap-5 px-6 mx-auto sm:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-8 lg:grid-cols-11 lg:grid-rows-6">
      {GEAR.map(({ label, name, image, colClass, imgClass, headingClass, labelSize }) => (
        <div class:list={[
          "relative p-4 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-100 border hover:border-muted-foreground/40 rounded-2xl border-muted-foreground/20 aspect-square group",
          colClass,
        ]}>
          <div class="transition-all duration-100 group-hover:translate-x-1">
            <span class:list={[
              "text-muted-foreground",
              labelSize === "xs" ? "text-xs" : "text-sm",
            ]}>{label}</span>
            <h5 class:list={[
              "font-bold leading-tight transition-all duration-100 opacity-25 group-hover:opacity-100",
              headingClass || "text-base md:text-lg",
            ]}>
              {name}
            </h5>
          </div>
          <div class:list={["absolute transition-all", imgClass]}>
            <img alt={name} class="h-full object-contain" src={image} />
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PLACES -->
  <section class="overflow-hidden mb-32">
    <header class="container max-w-2xl px-6 mx-auto mb-8">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-3xl">
        Cafes and Coffee places
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm md:text-base md:leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Home brewing is great and all but nothing can replace the sheer joy of heading
        over to your favorite third place to enjoy a nice cup of your usual cozy brew
        or to experiment something entirely new while being served by people with a lot
        to teach you both thanks to their different backgrounds in life, and to their
        vast experience preparing cups of java.
      </p>
    </header>

    <header class="container max-w-2xl px-6 mx-auto mb-4">
      <h5 class="text-base font-bold leading-tight md:text-lg">
        My third places
      </h5>
    </header>
    <div class="flex gap-4 overflow-x-scroll flex-nowrap justify-start md:px-[calc(50vw-21rem+24px)] px-4 pb-8 -mb-8">
      {PLACES.map(({ name, country, image, score }) => (
        <div class="flex flex-shrink-0 gap-3 p-1 border rounded-xl border-muted-foreground/20 w-80 md:w-96">
          <figure class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-lg w-28 h-36 bg-muted">
            <img alt={name} class="object-cover w-full h-full" src={image} />
          </figure>
          <div class="flex flex-col py-3">
            <span class="mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-bold leading-none uppercase text-muted-foreground">
              {country}
            </span>
            <h5 class="text-base font-bold leading-tight md:text-lg">
              {name}
            </h5>
            <div class="flex gap-2 mt-auto">
              <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground md:text-sm">⭐️ {score.toFixed(1)}</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THOUGHTS -->
  <section class="mb-32">
    <header class="container max-w-2xl px-6 mx-auto mb-8">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-3xl">
        Thinking about beans
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm md:text-base md:leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        So as per what's on the Thoughts page I've been getting quite passionate about
        writing and wanting to improve my writing abilities, that also projects itself
        in the coffee space. I've been learning a lot in the past months about these
        beautiful tasty beans and I'm looking forward to sharing my process and what I
        learn down the line somewhere a little more "formal", slowly but surely maturing
        my ability to articulate my thoughts about what I drink alongside my ability to
        actually taste and brew better cups.
      </p>
    </header>
  </section>
</Layout>